1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:03,128
Grocery stores put the milk as far from the door as possible.

2
00:00:03,328 --> 00:00:04,075
On purpose.

3
00:00:04,475 --> 00:00:06,117
Watch. Max needs one thing. Milk.

4
00:00:06,317 --> 00:00:08,899
He walks in, and bam! Fresh flowers and warm bread.

5
00:00:09,099 --> 00:00:10,571
Smells amazing. Into the cart.

6
00:00:10,971 --> 00:00:13,168
So where's the milk? All the way in the back corner.

7
00:00:13,368 --> 00:00:14,669
So he walks past the chips,

8
00:00:14,869 --> 00:00:16,149
past the free sample lady,

9
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:19,272
past cereal boxes with cartoon eyes staring right at him,

10
00:00:19,472 --> 00:00:21,840
past a giant tower of soda. Two for five!

11
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:23,512
Every aisle, the cart gets heavier.

12
00:00:23,912 --> 00:00:25,768
By the time he finally reaches the milk,

13
00:00:25,968 --> 00:00:26,864
his cart is full.

14
00:00:27,064 --> 00:00:29,304
And checkout? Candy and gum, right at eye level.

15
00:00:29,504 --> 00:00:31,659
He came in for a four dollar carton of milk,

16
00:00:31,859 --> 00:00:33,971
and walked out with sixty three dollars of stuff.

17
00:00:34,371 --> 00:00:35,949
That's the trick. The milk is the bait.

18
00:00:36,149 --> 00:00:40,608
Almost everyone needs it, so it goes in the back, and you walk past everything else to get it.

19
00:00:40,808 --> 00:00:44,093
Part of it is practical. The big coolers sit by the loading dock.

20
00:00:44,293 --> 00:00:48,837
And the pricey brands sit right at eye level, while the cheap ones hide down by your feet.

21
00:00:49,037 --> 00:00:52,067
But every extra step is one more chance to grab something.

22
00:00:52,467 --> 00:00:53,981
So next time you just need milk,

23
00:00:54,181 --> 00:00:55,675
walk in. Grab the milk. Get out.

